# Both images build from the project root, so without this file the whole
# working copy — Git history, build output, local secrets — is handed to the
# Docker daemon on every build.
#
# Deny everything, then admit the packages by their role suffix rather than by
# name: the list of packages is already written in the pubspecs, and a third
# copy here is one more place for a new or renamed package to be forgotten.
# `dartway deploy check` reads the Dockerfiles against the pubspecs and this
# file, and names a package that cannot reach its image.
**

!*_server/
!*_server/**
!*_flutter/
!*_flutter/**
!*_shared/
!*_shared/**

**/.dart_tool/
**/build/
**/.fvm/
**/ephemeral/
# custom_lint.log alone reaches hundreds of megabytes when the analyzer trips.
**/*.log
# The rendered server environment holds secrets; it never enters an image.
**/.env
